        <tr><td><strong>Sydney</strong></td><td class="num">3,013</td><td class="num">6.0%</td><td class="num">79.0%</td><td class="num">20.3%</td><td class="num">0.2%</td><td class="num">0.6%</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 2: PRICING ANALYSIS -->
<section>
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2>2. Pricing Dynamics Across Cities</h2>
    <p>Median and average nightly prices by city and room type</p>
  </div>

  <div class="warning-box">
    <strong>Price Data Limitation:</strong> Price values are completely missing for Paris (0/13,927) and Sydney (0/3,013). Among cities with price data, Bangkok's values appear to be denominated in Thai Baht (THB) rather than USD-equivalent, as a median of $1,400 USD would be anomalously high for Bangkok. The analysis below presents figures as they appear in the dataset, with this caveat noted.
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div class="card">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:16px;color:var(--primary);">Median Nightly Price by City</h3>
      <div class="chart-container">
        <canvas id="priceMedianChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
